# ============================================================================
# ritsu-works .env.per-human.example  —  CO-FOUNDER (admin / user) template
# ============================================================================
# Copy to runtime/secrets/.env.local (the co-founder install profile does this:
#   node scripts/local-install/install.cjs --profile=per-human --apply).
#
# This template DELIBERATELY OMITS every privileged / god key. A co-founder
# (admin or user tier) NEVER holds service_role, Stripe, or the bot tokens — that
# is the entire point of multi-user-auth: your blast radius = exactly your tier's
# SERVER-granted capabilities (per-tier RLS on ops.*, enforced by Supabase), and
# a leaked co-founder .env.local cannot bypass RLS or move money.
#
# HOW YOU GET IN (enrollment):
#   1. An OWNER runs `/users add <you> --tier=admin|user` + `invite.cjs <you> --tier=admin`
#      (creates your Supabase Auth identity + ops.operators row), then `mint.cjs <you>` and
#      sends you ONE token-based COMMAND. (DEFAULT, prefetch-proof delivery: a raw magic-link
#      URL gets auto-opened + consumed by chat/email/SafeLinks link-previews before you click it.)
#   2. Install per-human (node scripts/local-install/install.cjs --profile=per-human --apply),
#      fill SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_ANON_KEY below (ask the owner).
#   3. Complete enrollment by pasting the command the owner sent (byte-exact — don't retype tokens):
#         node scripts/multi-user-auth/enroll.cjs --refresh-token=<rt> --access-token=<at>
#      → it seeds the credential file below and redeems (invited→active) in one shot. Run it
#      promptly (the access token lives ~1h). Fallback: `enroll.cjs "<raw magic-link>"`.
#   4. `/test-ritsu-works` → verified ready. Your tier bounds everything.
# See 06-ai-ops/sops/SOP-AIOPS-017-multi-user-authz-contract/flow.yaml.
# NEVER share this file. It still authenticates AS YOU (your tier) — treat the
# refresh token as a live secret.
# ============================================================================

# === Deployment / runtime mode ===
RITSU_DEPLOYMENT_MODE=local
RITSU_WORKERS_LOCATION=local
RITSU_TELEGRAM_BOT_LOCATION=disabled
RITSU_MCP_SERVER_MODE=stdio
RITSU_MCP_HTTP_PORT=3001
RITSU_MCP_HTTP_URL=http://localhost:3001

# ============================================================================
# PER-HUMAN AUTH (required — this is how a co-founder connects)
# ============================================================================
# per-human: the MCP connects to ritsu-ops as `authenticated` with YOUR Supabase
# Auth credential (NOT service_role) and per-tier RLS enforces your tier server-side.
RITSU_AUTH_MODE=per-human

# The supabase-ops MCP is the SOLE token refresher; it re-persists your fresh
# access token here so per-human survives restarts. The analytics MCP + the gbrain
# tier-gate hook READ this file (read-only) to learn your verified tier.
# NOTE: `install --profile=per-human` AUTO-REWRITES this to an absolute path under
# YOUR clone (…/runtime/secrets/.operator-refresh.json) — you normally don't edit it.
# The placeholder below is only what ships in the template:
RITSU_OPERATOR_REFRESH_TOKEN_FILE=/Users/you/ritsu-works/runtime/secrets/.operator-refresh.json
# Inline seed only for the FIRST boot (the file above then becomes source of truth):
# RITSU_OPERATOR_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# ============================================================================
# Supabase (PUBLIC values only — NOT secrets)
# ============================================================================
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co   # the ritsu-ops project URL (ask the owner)
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGc...                         # the anon key is PUBLIC by design
# ⛔ NO SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY. service_role BYPASSES RLS — it is OWNER-ONLY. If you
#    were given one, do NOT use it; a co-founder never needs it (per-human RLS is
#    your access). Its absence here is intentional, not an omission.

# MCP_CALLER_ROLE is IGNORED in per-human mode (your tier comes from the verified
# JWT, and the HITL role-allowlist is skipped in favor of tier + RLS). Left unset.
# MCP_CALLER_ROLE=

# ============================================================================
# LLM Providers (OPTIONAL — your own keys, for autonomous skills)
# ============================================================================
# Subscription-only mode works with these empty (Claude Code does the LLM work).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ============================================================================
# Runtime config
# ============================================================================
RITSU_ENV=development
RITSU_LOG_LEVEL=info
RITSU_LOCALE_DEFAULT=vi
RITSU_TIMEZONE=Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh

# ── NOT PRESENT (owner-only; do not add them to a co-founder install) ──────────
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY   — bypasses RLS (god key)
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY / STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET — money movement
#   TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN / TWITTER_* / LINKEDIN_* / DISCORD_* / SLACK_* — brand channels
#   GITHUB_TOKEN with write scope — Tier-1 / merge (use your own `gh auth login` for PRs)
# If you need one of these, you need the OWNER tier — ask the owner; it is not a
# co-founder capability.
